menu "espforge core"

    config FORGE_DIAG_TASK_STATS
        bool "diag: per-task CPU and stack statistics at each report"
        default y
        help
            The "diag: tasks" and "diag: cpu" lines. They come from uxTaskGetSystemState(), which measures every task's
            stack with interrupts off: ~6 ms with 25 tasks on an ESP32-P4. A display whose driver restarts each frame
            from an interrupt (ESP-IDF's MIPI-DSI DPI panel: ~0.9 ms between frames) then misses a frame now and then
            and flashes white: turn this off there (MeteoBus's P4 port, October 2026; docs/LESSONS.md L201).

    config FORGE_DIAG_PSRAM_LARGEST
        bool "diag: PSRAM's largest free block in the heap line"
        default y
        help
            heap_caps_get_largest_free_block(MALLOC_CAP_SPIRAM) walks the whole PSRAM heap with interrupts off: ~2.3 ms
            with 32 MB. Off, the heap line keeps PSRAM's free size and minimum and prints "largest -" instead. Same
            reason as FORGE_DIAG_TASK_STATS. The starting log line "diag: stats cost" times both on this board.

endmenu
